<standOff type="wordsplit" corresp="#8NaṉC00154"><interp type="alignment" select="0">22MG14MG28MG11MG15M2GM,97M</interp>
<entry>
<form>yāṟṟu nīr</form>
<def>a mode of construing a verse in which the words are taken in their order without any transposition to yield the intended meaning</def>
<form type="sandhi">yāṟṟunīr</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>moḻi māṟṟu</form>
<def>a mode of construing a verse in which the words have to be transposed for the ascertainment of its proper meaning</def>
<form type="sandhi">moḻimāṟṟu</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>niral niṟai</form>
<def>a mode of construing a verse in which words are so arranged in groups that each term of one group is made to govern or qualify the corresponding term in another group</def>
<form type="sandhi">niraṉiṟai</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>vil pūṇ</form>
<def>a method of construing a verse by taking together the first and last words</def>
<form type="sandhi">viṟpūṇ</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>tāpp<c type="elided">u</c> icai</form>
<def>a mode of construing a word in the middle of a verse both with what precedes and what follows it</def>
<form type="sandhi">tāppicai</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form><c type="glide">y</c>aḷai maṟi pāppu<c type="geminated">k</c></form>
<def>a mode of construing in which the expression at the end of a verse is conjoined with a word in the middle of a verse or with one in the beginning of another verse,</def>
<form type="sandhi"><c type="glide">y</c>aḷaimaṟipāppu<c type="geminated">k</c></form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>koṇṭu kūṭṭ<c type="elided">u</c></form>
<def>a mode of construing a stanza in which words are appropriately transposed to arrive at the proper meaning</def>
<form type="sandhi">koṇṭukūṭṭ</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>aṭi maṟi māṟṟ<c type="elided">u</c></form>
<def>a mode of construing in which the lines of a verse have to change places to give the intended meaning, or can change places without the rhythm and meaning changing at the same time</def>
<form type="sandhi">aṭimaṟimāṟṟ</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>eṉa<c type="geminated">p</c></form>
<def>to say</def>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">infinitive</gram>
</gramGrp>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>poruḷ kōḷ</form>
<def>modes of construing verses, of which there are eight, viz., yāṟṟu-nīr, moḻi-māṟṟu, niraṉiṟai, viṟ-pūṇ, tāppicai, aḷai-maṟi-pāppu, koṇṭu-kūṭṭu, aṭimaṟi-māṟṟu</def>
<form type="sandhi">poruḷkōḷ</form>
</entry>
<entry>
<form>eṭṭ<c type="elided">u</c>-ē</form>
<def>eight</def>
<form type="simple">eṭṭu</form>
<form type="sandhi">eṭṭ</form>
<gramGrp>
  <gram type="role">noun</gram>
</gramGrp>
<gramGrp type="particle"><m type="enclitic">ē</m></gramGrp>
</entry></standOff>
